WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.182
Names with spaces, large files, and several people working at once all affect

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:08.367
uploads to the Media Library.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.676
Three features of the Media module handle them:

00:00:11.676 --> 00:00:15.298
Media Slugify, Media TUS Uploads, and Media SignalR.

00:00:15.298 --> 00:00:17.920
This video shows what each one does.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.898
By default, the Media Library keeps names as you type them, and spaces

00:00:26.898 --> 00:00:30.008
and symbols end up in the web address of a file.

00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:35.020
Media Slugify cleans the name of each folder you create and each file you upload.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.973
A large file takes time to upload, and a lost connection stops the default upload.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:44.935
Media TUS Uploads sends a file in parts, so you can pause it,

00:00:44.935 --> 00:00:48.010
resume it, and continue after an interruption.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.493
A Media Library open in one window does not update by itself when

00:00:53.493 --> 00:00:56.093
another window changes the files.

00:00:56.093 --> 00:01:01.360
Media SignalR keeps the file list of every open Media Library up to date.

00:01:05.588 --> 00:01:09.821
All three are features of the Media module, and all three are disabled

00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:11.381
until you enable them.

00:01:11.381 --> 00:01:14.278
Under Tools, Features, let's search for media.

00:01:14.731 --> 00:01:18.210
Let's enable Media Slugify, then Media TUS Uploads.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.360
After each one, a message at the top of the page confirms that

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.191
the feature was enabled.

00:01:24.644 --> 00:01:31.124
Media SignalR depends on the SignalR feature, so enabling Media SignalR also enables SignalR.

00:01:31.576 --> 00:01:38.141
Under Settings, Media, Options, Temporary file lifetime is the lifetime of the temporary

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:40.586
files that an upload creates.

00:01:40.586 --> 00:01:44.916
Further down, SignalR and TUS uploads show a check mark.

00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:56.389
Letters become lowercase, and spaces and most symbols between words become a single dash.

00:01:56.389 --> 00:02:01.978
The folder Images & docs is stored as images-docs, and the file The

00:02:01.978 --> 00:02:06.036
team (2020).jpg is stored as the-team-2020.jpg.

00:02:06.786 --> 00:02:10.286
The public address of a file is built from the stored names.

00:02:10.286 --> 00:02:14.209
Names that exist before you enable the feature stay as they are, and

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:15.906
so does a file you rename.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:23.548
In Media, Library, the folder Team Photos was created before Media Slugify was enabled.

00:02:23.548 --> 00:02:29.390
Its name, and the name of the file inside it, keep their capital letters and spaces.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.439
Let's create a folder.

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:35.300
The menu button of the Files folder offers Create a subfolder.

00:02:35.752 --> 00:02:38.906
Let's type Images & docs and select Ok.

00:02:38.906 --> 00:02:42.692
The folder tree lists the folder as images-docs.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:50.622
In images-docs, let's select Upload files and choose The team (2020).jpg.

00:02:50.622 --> 00:02:55.920
The list shows the stored name, the-team-2020.jpg.

00:02:56.385 --> 00:03:00.197
Two different names can give the same slug.

00:03:00.197 --> 00:03:06.499
With Media TUS Uploads enabled, a second picture named The Team 2020.jpg is

00:03:06.499 --> 00:03:11.245
saved as the-team-2020-1.jpg, with a number at the end.

00:03:15.438 --> 00:03:21.432
In the folder images-docs, Media TUS Uploads sends a file in parts.

00:03:21.432 --> 00:03:27.178
Let's upload a large file, retreat-video.mp4, with Upload files.

00:03:27.638 --> 00:03:32.641
The Uploads panel at the bottom right shows the progress and the speed of each file.

00:03:32.641 --> 00:03:36.978
If the connection breaks for a moment, the upload tries again by itself.

00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:39.793
The pause button stops the transfer.

00:03:39.793 --> 00:03:44.748
The progress bar stays where it is, and the parts already sent stay on the server.

00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:49.846
Selecting the button again, which shows a play icon, continues from that point

00:03:49.846 --> 00:03:51.557
instead of starting over.

00:03:51.557 --> 00:03:54.428
When the upload ends, the file is in the list.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.880
Closing the page keeps the parts already sent as well.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:05.080
Let's start another upload, office-tour.mp4, and reload the page while it is under way.

00:04:05.532 --> 00:04:10.187
Selecting the same file again continues the upload from the parts the server kept.

00:04:10.187 --> 00:04:12.832
The file joins the list once it is complete.

00:04:17.042 --> 00:04:21.408
Media SignalR connects each open Media Library to the server.

00:04:21.408 --> 00:04:26.882
The folder images-docs is open in this window, and in a second browser window.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:33.553
In the second window, let's upload summer-picnic.jpg to the same folder.

00:04:34.004 --> 00:04:37.934
Back in the first window, the file is already in the list, and

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.784
the page was not reloaded.

00:04:40.237 --> 00:04:44.834
Renaming, moving, copying and deleting a file are announced the same way.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:49.547
When the file is deleted in the other window, it disappears from this list.

00:04:50.021 --> 00:04:53.925
Updates cover the files of the folder you are viewing, and only for

00:04:53.925 --> 00:04:56.065
folders you are allowed to manage.

00:04:56.065 --> 00:05:00.344
Without Media SignalR, a window shows the changes of others only after you

00:05:00.344 --> 00:05:02.431
reload the page or open a folder.

00:05:06.631 --> 00:05:11.097
By default, a resumable upload keeps its parts in a temporary folder and

00:05:11.097 --> 00:05:12.815
its progress in a cache.

00:05:12.815 --> 00:05:16.767
On several servers, all the parts of a file must reach the same

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:21.291
server, or the servers must share the folder and the Redis Cache feature.

00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:29.346
Live updates need a backplane, which the SignalR Azure Backplane or SignalR Redis Backplane feature provides.

00:05:29.346 --> 00:05:34.111
Without one, updates reach only windows connected to the same server.

00:05:36.111 --> 00:05:41.360
Media Slugify cleans the names of folders and files, Media TUS Uploads makes

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.186
large uploads resumable, and Media SignalR keeps every open Media Library up to date.

00:05:47.186 --> 00:05:48.851
Thanks for watching.

